1
00:00:00,834 --> 00:00:03,044
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:10,969 --> 00:00:13,722
<i>Once I return to Poblacion Ardiente,</i>

3
00:00:13,805 --> 00:00:18,893
<i>I will clean up the trash that</i>
<i>gathered there while I was away.</i>

4
00:00:18,977 --> 00:00:22,439
[Emilia] <i>I don't understand!</i>
<i>Why can't he just die?!</i>

5
00:00:22,522 --> 00:00:26,901
<i>He will regret coming back here</i>
<i>to Poblacion Ardiente.</i>

6
00:00:26,985 --> 00:00:28,319
<i>Mayor, some of our men saw Miss Aguas</i>

7
00:00:28,403 --> 00:00:30,613
<i>leave right after Mr. Raul.</i>

8
00:00:30,697 --> 00:00:31,614
-[screams]
-[glass shatters]

9
00:00:32,032 --> 00:00:34,367
-[Belen] <i>Raul, Jasmin got away!</i>
<i>-Where is Jasmin?!</i>

10
00:00:34,451 --> 00:00:35,869
-[Belen] <i>Look for her!</i>
-[tires screech]

11
00:00:35,952 --> 00:00:38,705
<i>Mom? Mom, it's me. It's me, Lily.</i>

12
00:00:38,997 --> 00:00:41,041
<i>I'm sure it was her.</i>

13
00:00:41,124 --> 00:00:43,877
<i>But she ran from me.</i>
<i>I couldn't catch up to her.</i>

14
00:00:43,960 --> 00:00:45,503
<i>But I'm sure that was my mom.</i>

15
00:00:45,879 --> 00:00:50,133
<i>I'm confused if she's referring</i>
<i>to Prianka Aguas or Camia Cruz.</i>

16
00:00:50,216 --> 00:00:53,178
<i>I have a hunch that Ivy</i>
<i>and Lily are the same person.</i>

17
00:00:53,261 --> 00:00:55,972
-[Raul] <i>I have to hide Camia.</i>
<i>-Camia? Who is Camia?</i>

18
00:00:56,056 --> 00:00:57,974
[Emilia] <i>I don't like women</i>
<i>flirting with my husband.</i>

19
00:00:58,058 --> 00:01:00,101
<i>I don't intend on tainting my reputation</i>

20
00:01:00,185 --> 00:01:02,520
<i>by sleeping with your useless husband.</i>

21
00:01:02,604 --> 00:01:04,981
<i>Project your insecurity</i>
<i>elsewhere, but not on me.</i>

22
00:01:05,065 --> 00:01:07,692
[Belen] <i>He told me her name was Jasmin.</i>

23
00:01:07,776 --> 00:01:08,818
<i>Raul left with Camia last night</i>

24
00:01:08,902 --> 00:01:10,403
<i>and went somewhere far away.</i>

25
00:01:10,487 --> 00:01:13,156
-[Ivy] <i>Raul Torillo?</i>
<i>-He has Camia.</i>

26
00:01:13,865 --> 00:01:15,742
[Emilia] <i>I missed you. Welcome back!</i>

27
00:01:15,825 --> 00:01:19,788
[Julio] <i>You can't fool me</i>
<i>with your crocodile tears,</i>

28
00:01:19,871 --> 00:01:21,247
<i>hugs, and kisses.</i>

29
00:01:21,331 --> 00:01:24,834
<i>I know what you've been doing.</i>

30
00:01:24,918 --> 00:01:28,129
<i>This is not happening, right?</i>
<i>This can't be happening!</i>

31
00:01:28,213 --> 00:01:29,881
<i>He cannot take everything away from me!</i>

32
00:01:29,964 --> 00:01:30,924
<i>He cannot do this to me!</i>

33
00:01:31,007 --> 00:01:32,717
<i>-Auntie, I cannot win!</i>
<i>-Calm down, Emilia.</i>

34
00:01:32,801 --> 00:01:35,637
<i>You can't allow Julio to smell your fear!</i>

35
00:01:35,720 --> 00:01:37,138
<i>That was the downfall of your mother.</i>

36
00:01:37,222 --> 00:01:40,266
<i>And I'll be damned</i>
<i>if I let that happen to you!</i>

37
00:01:40,350 --> 00:01:43,853
<i>He may be Julio Ardiente,</i>
<i>but he's only just a man!</i>

38
00:01:43,937 --> 00:01:45,855
<i>Do you understand me?!</i>

39
00:01:50,777 --> 00:01:53,071
[Carlotta] You have to
wash this again, okay?

40
00:01:53,154 --> 00:01:54,948
-[maid] Okay.
-All right. Make sure of that.

41
00:01:59,369 --> 00:02:01,037
[breathes heavily]

42
00:02:01,121 --> 00:02:02,372
-[Ivy screams]
-Dear!

43
00:02:03,331 --> 00:02:04,624
That monster!

44
00:02:04,707 --> 00:02:08,920
[panting] That animal, Raul,
has my mother.

45
00:02:09,003 --> 00:02:13,800
Ivy, you can save your mother.
You <i>will</i> save your mother.

46
00:02:13,883 --> 00:02:15,426
I know I will.

47
00:02:15,510 --> 00:02:19,055
I'll save my mother from that
bastard, Nanny Carlotta.

48
00:02:19,139 --> 00:02:20,515
[quietly] Yes, you will.

49
00:02:21,224 --> 00:02:23,017
-Where's Jepoy?!
-Uh…

50
00:02:25,395 --> 00:02:26,938
-[Carlotta] Dear…
-Ivy.

51
00:02:27,021 --> 00:02:29,566
Jepoy, we were right. Our hunch was right!

52
00:02:29,816 --> 00:02:32,026
That animal, Raul, has my mother, Jepoy!

53
00:02:32,235 --> 00:02:34,529
Go back to the Ardientes!

54
00:02:34,612 --> 00:02:36,698
We'll communicate through
our cell phones for now.

55
00:02:36,781 --> 00:02:40,618
When Raul goes back to the
Ardientes, update me right away.

56
00:02:41,035 --> 00:02:42,829
We need to keep a closer eye on Raul.

57
00:02:42,912 --> 00:02:46,082
He's the key to saving my mother.

58
00:02:46,166 --> 00:02:48,084
So, I can see her again.

59
00:02:49,669 --> 00:02:51,254
Of all people!

60
00:02:51,713 --> 00:02:56,050
That bastard, Raul! He has my mother.

61
00:02:56,551 --> 00:02:58,136
You'll be with your mother again, Ivy.

62
00:02:58,219 --> 00:02:59,596
-I'm sure of that.
-Yes, you will.

63
00:02:59,679 --> 00:03:05,351
Yes, I'll be with her again.
I'll save her from that bastard!

64
00:03:05,894 --> 00:03:10,148
[tense music playing]

65
00:03:15,945 --> 00:03:16,946
Jasmin?

66
00:03:18,072 --> 00:03:21,117
Jasmin. Here's your food.

67
00:03:22,619 --> 00:03:27,457
I cooked it myself, so you'd feel better.

68
00:03:36,049 --> 00:03:37,175
Jasmin?

69
00:03:39,219 --> 00:03:44,015
I know you're upset with me
because of what I did,

70
00:03:44,098 --> 00:03:48,186
but I only did it to protect you.

71
00:03:48,645 --> 00:03:49,604
And…

72
00:03:50,063 --> 00:03:51,022
[Raul clicks tongue]

73
00:03:54,567 --> 00:03:55,693
Jasmin, I'm sorry.

74
00:03:58,446 --> 00:04:01,282
I love you very much.
I'll never… I'll never…

75
00:04:03,284 --> 00:04:05,870
I'll never hurt you again. Believe me.

76
00:04:06,079 --> 00:04:09,707
Eat now, Jasmin. We'll be okay here.

77
00:04:09,791 --> 00:04:13,461
[sobs, screams]

78
00:04:13,544 --> 00:04:16,881
-Jasmin. Jasmin, wait!
-[screaming, sobbing]

79
00:04:17,090 --> 00:04:18,758
-Jasmin.
-[Jasmin panting]

80
00:04:19,634 --> 00:04:20,635
[sighs]

81
00:04:21,135 --> 00:04:24,681
[panting]

82
00:04:28,518 --> 00:04:29,811
That's enough.

83
00:04:30,979 --> 00:04:32,855
Jasmin, that's enough.

84
00:04:34,899 --> 00:04:36,567
I'm here for you.

85
00:04:36,651 --> 00:04:39,988
I won't leave you. Calm down.

86
00:04:40,071 --> 00:04:42,448
Nobody will get in between us.

87
00:04:47,412 --> 00:04:48,913
-[Camia] <i>Sir, excuse me.</i>
-[Raul] <i>Wait…</i>

88
00:04:48,997 --> 00:04:51,833
[Camia] <i>Sir, please don't… Don't touch me!</i>

89
00:04:54,627 --> 00:04:58,214
[sobs, screams]

90
00:04:58,298 --> 00:05:02,677
-[screaming continues]
-Jasmin!

91
00:05:04,053 --> 00:05:06,514
-[Jasmin screaming]
-Jasmin.

92
00:05:08,308 --> 00:05:14,772
[Jasmin screaming, sobbing]

93
00:05:17,567 --> 00:05:24,365
-Calm down. Calm down.
-[sobbing continues]

94
00:05:24,449 --> 00:05:25,950
[Raul shushes]

95
00:05:26,367 --> 00:05:28,745
[sobbing continues]

96
00:05:29,996 --> 00:05:33,666
-[shushes] Calm down.
-[Jasmin sobbing]

97
00:05:34,042 --> 00:05:37,211
-[stutters] I won't--
-[Jasmin sobbing]

98
00:05:37,545 --> 00:05:39,714
-[sobbing continues]
-[Raul shushes]

99
00:05:43,509 --> 00:05:44,343
[Raul sniffles]

100
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:52,477
[dramatic tense music playing]

101
00:05:54,771 --> 00:05:55,772
[birds chirping]

102
00:06:01,027 --> 00:06:02,278
Hey, Nanny, Uncle!

103
00:06:02,820 --> 00:06:04,155
-[giggling]
-I didn't see you there.

104
00:06:05,448 --> 00:06:06,449
How do I look?

105
00:06:06,991 --> 00:06:07,992
Great!

106
00:06:08,076 --> 00:06:11,704
That's the Diego we know.
He never gives up.

107
00:06:12,872 --> 00:06:17,960
Well, I realized that it
doesn't matter if Ivy is Lily.

108
00:06:18,836 --> 00:06:22,715
For now, I won't worry about
all the secrets she's keeping.

109
00:06:24,217 --> 00:06:28,888
[exhales sharply] What's
important is how I feel for her.

110
00:06:29,555 --> 00:06:31,224
That's what will set us free.

111
00:06:32,183 --> 00:06:34,060
No matter how many times
she turns me down--

112
00:06:34,143 --> 00:06:37,355
-You'll never say die!
-[laughter]

113
00:06:37,897 --> 00:06:39,941
[exhales] I love her.

114
00:06:43,736 --> 00:06:44,987
Excuse me. [knocking]

115
00:06:45,613 --> 00:06:48,074
Oh! Hi, Mayor! Please come in.

116
00:06:52,286 --> 00:06:56,582
Um… You probably heard
that Grandpa is back.

117
00:06:57,416 --> 00:06:58,668
He sent me to fetch you.

118
00:07:00,795 --> 00:07:02,130
What if I don't go?

119
00:07:03,089 --> 00:07:05,675
What if I don't let you? Come on.

120
00:07:05,758 --> 00:07:07,927
Grandpa sent your beloved
brother here to fetch you

121
00:07:08,010 --> 00:07:09,804
and make sure you'll come.

122
00:07:20,064 --> 00:07:21,858
[tense music playing]

123
00:07:21,941 --> 00:07:22,942
[Julio] Emilia.

124
00:07:25,486 --> 00:07:27,697
Have a seat, Papa.

125
00:07:28,781 --> 00:07:29,949
[laughs]

126
00:07:31,409 --> 00:07:32,326
[Julio grunts]

127
00:07:36,205 --> 00:07:37,582
[Julio groans]

128
00:07:41,794 --> 00:07:42,795
Well?

129
00:07:44,297 --> 00:07:45,965
Why are you just standing there?

130
00:07:46,174 --> 00:07:47,175
Sit down.

131
00:07:51,387 --> 00:07:53,890
You're like a mushroom, Clarita.

132
00:07:55,224 --> 00:07:57,810
You popped up out of nowhere.

133
00:07:59,437 --> 00:08:02,398
You even chose to show up
just when I wasn't here.

134
00:08:04,859 --> 00:08:08,905
Anyway… why isn't Miss Aguas here?

135
00:08:09,947 --> 00:08:12,033
Why isn't she here to welcome me?

136
00:08:12,992 --> 00:08:14,243
She's busy, Papa.

137
00:08:17,288 --> 00:08:20,458
Oh! Is she, Emilia?

138
00:08:21,417 --> 00:08:24,337
With what? Playing you for a sap?

139
00:08:27,298 --> 00:08:30,468
[Julio laughs] Oh, Emilia!

140
00:08:30,551 --> 00:08:33,387
You never did learn to use your brain.

141
00:08:34,639 --> 00:08:37,099
-Julio, that's enough.
-No one tells me what to do!

142
00:08:38,267 --> 00:08:40,478
And I certainly won't take it from you.

143
00:08:41,270 --> 00:08:45,441
Have you forgotten that you're
just a guest here in my home?!

144
00:08:48,653 --> 00:08:49,946
And you, Emilia.

145
00:08:50,821 --> 00:08:53,407
You allowed Ivy to toy around with you

146
00:08:53,491 --> 00:08:54,951
in the palm of her hand.

147
00:08:56,619 --> 00:08:57,995
Well, that stops now!

148
00:08:58,829 --> 00:09:01,749
From now on,
I'll be the one to talk to Ivy.

149
00:09:04,043 --> 00:09:07,964
I'll make her pay for
everything she owes me.

150
00:09:09,507 --> 00:09:10,633
Arnaldo.

151
00:09:14,053 --> 00:09:19,517
Pick Miss Aguas up tomorrow, and
tell her I want to talk to her.

152
00:09:21,060 --> 00:09:22,061
Yes, Grandpa.

153
00:09:22,812 --> 00:09:25,106
It's time to find out

154
00:09:25,398 --> 00:09:28,776
if that woman is with us or against us.

155
00:09:31,946 --> 00:09:37,243
You know very well what happens
to our family's enemies, right?

156
00:09:37,326 --> 00:09:38,953
[suspenseful sting]

157
00:09:39,036 --> 00:09:42,790
[tense music playing]

158
00:09:44,792 --> 00:09:48,129
Now where is that husband
of yours, Emilia?

159
00:09:49,380 --> 00:09:55,803
Why isn't he here?
Isn't he glad that I'm back?

160
00:09:58,097 --> 00:10:02,393
Well… Maybe it's better
he isn't here because…

161
00:10:03,936 --> 00:10:07,148
who knows what could happen
to him now that I'm back.

162
00:10:09,191 --> 00:10:10,693
What are you planning to do to Dad?

163
00:10:10,776 --> 00:10:12,653
He didn't do anything to you!

164
00:10:13,779 --> 00:10:15,656
[laughs]

165
00:10:16,282 --> 00:10:17,867
Hasn't your mother told you yet?

166
00:10:21,329 --> 00:10:23,789
Papa, please not now.

167
00:10:24,624 --> 00:10:26,042
Why, Emilia?

168
00:10:26,834 --> 00:10:31,088
What are you afraid
your sons will find out?

169
00:10:35,092 --> 00:10:41,432
That your no-good husband
is a worthless piece of--

170
00:10:41,515 --> 00:10:45,019
Grandpa… Grandpa… Think about your heart.

171
00:10:46,771 --> 00:10:50,358
[tense music playing]

172
00:10:52,818 --> 00:10:56,405
I didn't come here to listen
to you insult my father!

173
00:10:58,574 --> 00:10:59,700
I'm leaving.

174
00:11:03,871 --> 00:11:05,539
Before you go, Diego.

175
00:11:08,167 --> 00:11:09,752
I want you to remember…

176
00:11:10,836 --> 00:11:14,048
Even if you no longer live in this house,

177
00:11:14,131 --> 00:11:17,385
you still have duties to fulfill.

178
00:11:18,135 --> 00:11:20,179
Because in the eyes of the public,

179
00:11:20,262 --> 00:11:27,853
this family is complete, happy,
and loves one another.

180
00:11:27,937 --> 00:11:30,356
And it will stay that way!

181
00:11:30,940 --> 00:11:36,153
And now that I'm back, we will
repair this family's image.

182
00:11:38,864 --> 00:11:40,825
I'm done pretending for you, Grandpa.

183
00:11:41,659 --> 00:11:43,953
And I am willing to protect all
the important people…

184
00:11:44,537 --> 00:11:46,497
in my life from this family!

185
00:11:47,665 --> 00:11:51,377
[tense music intensifies]

186
00:11:55,339 --> 00:11:58,467
[tense music playing]

187
00:12:03,389 --> 00:12:05,808
Well then, let's eat.

188
00:12:10,771 --> 00:12:12,481
[cutlery clinking]

189
00:12:14,775 --> 00:12:17,528
[tense music playing]

190
00:12:20,656 --> 00:12:23,033
Where could Raul have taken my mother?

191
00:12:25,035 --> 00:12:31,876
Ivy, aside from his Aunt Belen,
maybe Raul has other relatives.

192
00:12:45,806 --> 00:12:46,807
[Ivy exhales]

193
00:12:49,768 --> 00:12:52,521
[phone ringing]

194
00:12:53,772 --> 00:12:56,400
[phone ringing]

195
00:12:58,152 --> 00:13:00,946
-Ivy.
-Jepoy, any news on Raul?

196
00:13:01,780 --> 00:13:03,199
He didn't show up here.

197
00:13:03,282 --> 00:13:04,783
And it looks like he's never going to.

198
00:13:04,867 --> 00:13:08,245
-What makes you say that?
-Julio's back, Ivy.

199
00:13:09,663 --> 00:13:11,832
Señor Julio has returned

200
00:13:11,916 --> 00:13:13,501
<i>to Poblacion Ardiente.</i>

201
00:13:13,584 --> 00:13:16,587
We have to be more careful.

202
00:13:16,670 --> 00:13:19,548
I'll speed up my search
for my mother, Jepoy.

203
00:13:20,382 --> 00:13:23,093
And you… You are on the Ardientes' turf.

204
00:13:23,177 --> 00:13:24,053
Be careful.

205
00:13:24,136 --> 00:13:28,057
-Ivy, I'll help you.
-Thank you.

206
00:13:28,807 --> 00:13:29,975
<i>Let's keep in touch.</i>

207
00:13:30,684 --> 00:13:31,560
Goodbye.

208
00:13:31,644 --> 00:13:32,686
Bye.

209
00:13:33,771 --> 00:13:37,566
[tense music playing]

210
00:13:44,990 --> 00:13:46,742
I'll give Papa his medication.

211
00:13:46,951 --> 00:13:47,993
Okay, ma'am.

212
00:13:53,040 --> 00:13:55,417
-Papa.
-[scoffs] Emilia.

213
00:13:56,877 --> 00:14:01,382
You wouldn't try to poison
me again, would you?

214
00:14:02,967 --> 00:14:06,303
Just like what you did
when we were in America.

215
00:14:07,304 --> 00:14:10,808
[clicks tongue] It's a good
thing my nurse was sharp

216
00:14:10,891 --> 00:14:17,523
and noticed the poison you tried
to pass off as my medication.

217
00:14:21,652 --> 00:14:27,700
What? Oh, come on! Cat got your tongue?

218
00:14:28,909 --> 00:14:30,244
Aren't you going to deny it?

219
00:14:34,623 --> 00:14:37,751
You must be so proud or callous…

220
00:14:39,795 --> 00:14:42,840
to try and kill your own father.

221
00:14:44,758 --> 00:14:49,305
What would Arnaldo say
if he found out about that?

222
00:14:51,056 --> 00:14:57,146
Or if he finds out
that his father strangled me,

223
00:14:57,229 --> 00:14:58,689
which led me to have a heart attack,

224
00:14:58,772 --> 00:15:00,190
almost killing me in the process.

225
00:15:07,865 --> 00:15:09,199
What do you think?

226
00:15:10,326 --> 00:15:11,660
Don't you dare, Julio.

227
00:15:12,661 --> 00:15:15,122
If I let you hurt my sister back then…

228
00:15:15,414 --> 00:15:17,416
not now. Not with Emilia!

229
00:15:19,919 --> 00:15:21,545
[laughs]

230
00:15:23,547 --> 00:15:27,259
Looks like my brilliant
daughter found herself an ally.

231
00:15:28,677 --> 00:15:29,929
Well, it doesn't matter.

232
00:15:31,096 --> 00:15:36,894
Remember, anyone who
opposes me will be punished.

233
00:15:39,021 --> 00:15:40,064
And you, Emilia…

234
00:15:42,524 --> 00:15:44,318
I'll make you suffer.

235
00:15:47,196 --> 00:15:51,992
You'll see just how cruel
your father can be.

236
00:15:53,577 --> 00:15:57,498
[tense music playing]

237
00:16:03,837 --> 00:16:05,047
[whispers] Emilia.

238
00:16:07,508 --> 00:16:10,970
[tense music playing]

239
00:16:27,444 --> 00:16:28,445
[engine stops]

240
00:16:34,785 --> 00:16:38,539
[soft music playing]

241
00:16:40,290 --> 00:16:41,625
[doorbell rings]

242
00:16:49,967 --> 00:16:51,301
-[doorbell rings]
-It's Diego.

243
00:16:53,345 --> 00:16:54,930
-[Ivy sighs]
-[quietly] I'll get it.

244
00:16:59,143 --> 00:17:00,144
[door opens]

245
00:17:01,145 --> 00:17:03,188
-Diego.
-Miss Carlotta.

246
00:17:03,772 --> 00:17:05,607
-[Carlotta] Yes, Diego?
-[Diego] Good evening.

247
00:17:05,691 --> 00:17:06,775
[Carlotta] Good evening.

248
00:17:06,900 --> 00:17:08,736
Can I talk to Ivy?

249
00:17:08,819 --> 00:17:11,280
Oh, no. She's asleep.

250
00:17:11,363 --> 00:17:12,781
She went to bed early.

251
00:17:13,240 --> 00:17:14,450
Miss Carlotta, please.

252
00:17:14,867 --> 00:17:17,119
I have something important to tell her.

253
00:17:17,453 --> 00:17:18,912
[Carlotta] You can leave her a message.

254
00:17:18,996 --> 00:17:20,873
I'll just relay it to her, Diego.

255
00:17:24,334 --> 00:17:25,377
[sighs]

256
00:17:25,961 --> 00:17:28,630
Grandpa wants to meet with her tomorrow.

257
00:17:29,256 --> 00:17:32,634
Please tell her to be careful
and not to go with them.

258
00:17:34,344 --> 00:17:37,973
All right. I'll tell her. Thank you.

259
00:17:39,975 --> 00:17:42,394
And one more thing…

260
00:17:46,482 --> 00:17:47,608
Um…

261
00:17:49,485 --> 00:17:51,028
Please give these to her.

262
00:17:52,738 --> 00:17:53,781
[Carlotta] Of course.

263
00:17:57,076 --> 00:17:58,077
Thank you.

264
00:17:59,787 --> 00:18:00,829
Thank you too.

265
00:18:02,331 --> 00:18:03,415
Bye.

266
00:18:03,499 --> 00:18:05,501
-Thanks again.
-All right. Goodnight.

267
00:18:05,584 --> 00:18:06,794
[Carlotta] Goodnight.

268
00:18:15,969 --> 00:18:16,804
[door closes]

269
00:18:18,263 --> 00:18:21,683
[soft music playing]

270
00:18:27,815 --> 00:18:29,399
He asked me to give you this.

271
00:18:36,115 --> 00:18:40,119
[soft music playing]

272
00:18:40,786 --> 00:18:42,621
You know what to do with that, Nanny.

273
00:18:44,206 --> 00:18:45,165
Ivy.

274
00:18:45,833 --> 00:18:48,460
How long are you going to avoid Diego?

275
00:18:51,255 --> 00:18:53,507
I don't have time to think
about Diego right now, Nanny.

276
00:18:54,675 --> 00:18:59,721
What's more important to me…
is I find my mother.

277
00:19:00,806 --> 00:19:05,018
And I also need to make sure
all my loved ones are safe…

278
00:19:05,936 --> 00:19:09,189
from the Ardientes. That's my priority.

279
00:19:19,783 --> 00:19:23,829
[soft guitar music playing]

280
00:19:24,663 --> 00:19:26,081
[Diego] <i>I can't explain it.</i>

281
00:19:27,791 --> 00:19:35,048
<i>Whenever we're together,</i>
<i>I feel like I'm with Lily again.</i>

282
00:19:39,344 --> 00:19:41,763
<i>Did you ever have a</i>
<i>best friend when you were a kid?</i>

283
00:19:41,847 --> 00:19:43,098
<i>I was a loner.</i>

284
00:19:43,599 --> 00:19:45,601
<i>I was always cooped up in my room.</i>

285
00:19:46,435 --> 00:19:47,978
<i>All I did was read.</i>

286
00:19:48,145 --> 00:19:51,607
<i>Really? I love to read too.</i>
<i>Just like Lily.</i>

287
00:19:51,732 --> 00:19:53,358
<i>Do you know </i>The Count of Monte Cristo<i>?</i>

288
00:19:56,028 --> 00:19:58,614
[Ivy] <i>"Moral wounds have this peculiarity.</i>

289
00:19:59,531 --> 00:20:03,869
<i>They may be hidden, but they never close."</i>

290
00:20:05,120 --> 00:20:08,832
[Diego] <i>"Always painful, always</i>
<i>ready to bleed when touched,</i>

291
00:20:09,958 --> 00:20:13,295
<i>they remain fresh and open in the heart."</i>

292
00:20:13,629 --> 00:20:15,881
[young Diego] <i>Why do you</i>
<i>always have that with you?</i>

293
00:20:15,964 --> 00:20:17,633
The Count of Monte Cristo.

294
00:20:17,883 --> 00:20:20,260
<i>I love it when my father reads this to me.</i>

295
00:20:25,891 --> 00:20:27,351
<i>Ivy, what happened?</i>

296
00:20:27,601 --> 00:20:28,602
<i>My mom…</i>

297
00:20:28,685 --> 00:20:30,520
<i>Ivy, Prianka's been dead for years.</i>

298
00:20:30,854 --> 00:20:35,484
<i>I'm confused if she's referring</i>
<i>to Prianka Aguas or Camia Cruz.</i>

299
00:20:36,026 --> 00:20:39,738
<i>I have a hunch that Ivy</i>
<i>and Lily are the same person.</i>

300
00:20:41,406 --> 00:20:43,075
<i>Ivy, I didn't know you had a sister.</i>

301
00:20:43,158 --> 00:20:45,786
<i>Why didn't you tell me?</i>
<i>Why are you keeping secrets?</i>

302
00:20:45,953 --> 00:20:47,120
<i>I didn't tell you about her</i>

303
00:20:47,204 --> 00:20:49,206
<i>because it's still a very</i>
<i>sensitive topic for me.</i>

304
00:20:49,289 --> 00:20:51,375
<i>I guess you won't understand</i>

305
00:20:51,458 --> 00:20:53,252
<i>because you've never lost</i>
<i>a loved one before.</i>

306
00:20:53,335 --> 00:20:55,212
<i>I know the feeling. I've lost someone too.</i>

307
00:20:55,295 --> 00:20:58,840
<i>Diego, Lily just disappeared,</i>
<i>she didn't die.</i>

308
00:20:58,924 --> 00:20:59,967
<i>They're different things.</i>

309
00:21:00,259 --> 00:21:03,512
[Loring] <i>Maybe you're</i>
<i>falling in love with Miss Ivy</i>

310
00:21:03,595 --> 00:21:05,847
<i>because you think that she's Lily.</i>

311
00:21:06,056 --> 00:21:07,849
<i>What if that's not true?</i>

312
00:21:07,933 --> 00:21:11,061
<i>Would you still be in love with Miss Ivy?</i>

313
00:21:15,357 --> 00:21:19,403
[soft guitar music playing]

314
00:21:31,331 --> 00:21:35,335
[soft guitar music playing]

315
00:21:54,980 --> 00:21:59,067
[soft instrumental music playing]

316
00:22:27,137 --> 00:22:30,265
[Ivy] <i>I know I make a lot</i>
<i>of risky decisions.</i>

317
00:22:30,348 --> 00:22:34,186
<i>Decisions that make you</i>
<i>worry. But you're still here.</i>

318
00:22:34,728 --> 00:22:38,607
<i>To be honest, you do so much for me.</i>

319
00:22:38,857 --> 00:22:40,859
<i>Sometimes, you risk your life</i>

320
00:22:40,942 --> 00:22:43,070
<i>because you're one of Arnaldo's men,</i>

321
00:22:43,445 --> 00:22:45,155
<i>but you still continue to help me.</i>

322
00:22:45,238 --> 00:22:46,323
<i>You're always there for me.</i>

323
00:22:46,406 --> 00:22:49,159
<i>You're a good friend, Jepoy.</i>

324
00:22:55,457 --> 00:22:58,502
[Jepoy] <i>You're not mad he kissed</i>
<i>you? Ivy, he disrespected you!</i>

325
00:22:58,585 --> 00:23:01,671
<i>I hit him right after</i>
<i>if that's what you want to hear.</i>

326
00:23:01,755 --> 00:23:04,132
<i>That's not enough!</i>
<i>I could beat him to a pulp.</i>

327
00:23:04,216 --> 00:23:05,717
<i>Break a few bones if you want!</i>

328
00:23:05,801 --> 00:23:07,677
<i>Wait, why are you acting like this?</i>

329
00:23:08,261 --> 00:23:11,389
<i>Ivy, I just want to protect</i>
<i>you from the Ardientes.</i>

330
00:23:12,057 --> 00:23:13,517
<i>Especially from those brothers!</i>

331
00:23:21,733 --> 00:23:25,612
[tense music playing]

332
00:23:28,323 --> 00:23:31,910
[Julio] <i>She's smart. She's beautiful.</i>

333
00:23:35,831 --> 00:23:37,791
<i>Financially independent.</i>

334
00:23:37,874 --> 00:23:42,003
<i>Looks like my perception</i>
<i>of women is starting to change.</i>

335
00:23:42,295 --> 00:23:45,090
[Emilia] <i>I know that you've been</i>
<i>lusting after Ivy the minute</i>

336
00:23:45,173 --> 00:23:47,008
<i>that you laid your eyes on her.</i>

337
00:23:47,384 --> 00:23:50,679
[Arnaldo] <i>No target has ever</i>
<i>escaped my trap.</i>

338
00:23:51,847 --> 00:23:55,976
<i>No matter what happens,</i>
<i>you will be mine, Ivy.</i>

339
00:23:57,686 --> 00:24:02,023
[tense music playing]

340
00:24:03,692 --> 00:24:06,611
<i>From now on, I'll be the one</i>
<i>to talk to Ivy.</i>

341
00:24:06,987 --> 00:24:12,784
<i>It's time to find out if that</i>
<i>woman is with us or against us.</i>

342
00:24:19,082 --> 00:24:22,836
[tense music playing]

343
00:24:32,637 --> 00:24:34,431
[Prianka] <i>So, what do you want, Lily?</i>

344
00:24:34,514 --> 00:24:38,185
<i>I want justice for my mom and dad!</i>

345
00:24:38,268 --> 00:24:39,477
<i>Then, we have a deal.</i>

346
00:24:39,936 --> 00:24:45,108
[Prianka] <i>Remember everything</i>
<i>I taught you.</i>

347
00:24:47,152 --> 00:24:50,197
<i>Do what you must do.</i>

348
00:24:52,282 --> 00:24:54,284
<i>Make them pay!</i>

349
00:24:54,367 --> 00:24:55,493
<i>Miss Prianka.</i>

350
00:25:01,833 --> 00:25:04,544
[tense music playing]

351
00:25:07,005 --> 00:25:11,801
<i>I wouldn't be where I am today</i>
<i>if not for you, Miss Prianka.</i>

352
00:25:11,885 --> 00:25:14,095
<i>Fate's a funny thing.</i>

353
00:25:14,721 --> 00:25:16,389
<i>But in the end, it was still your guidance</i>

354
00:25:16,473 --> 00:25:19,309
<i>that led me to find my mother.</i>

355
00:25:19,976 --> 00:25:23,813
<i>I promise I won't fail.</i>

356
00:25:26,858 --> 00:25:30,195
-[Emilia sobbing]
-This can't be, Emilia.

357
00:25:33,240 --> 00:25:35,909
[sobbing] Auntie, this can't happen!

358
00:25:35,992 --> 00:25:37,619
This can't happen!

359
00:25:38,745 --> 00:25:41,581
I don't know what Papa might do to me,

360
00:25:41,665 --> 00:25:44,167
you, and worst of all, Raul!

361
00:25:46,503 --> 00:25:47,796
Look at me, Emilia.

362
00:25:49,589 --> 00:25:51,758
I'll take care of Julio for you.

363
00:25:54,344 --> 00:25:57,389
I am willing to go
to such lengths for you.

364
00:25:58,932 --> 00:26:04,980
After what he did to my sister,
I can never forgive him!

365
00:26:11,653 --> 00:26:19,536
Auntie, I need you now.
I need someone on my side.

366
00:26:20,495 --> 00:26:22,747
I need you more now, Auntie.

367
00:26:26,751 --> 00:26:28,295
We can do this, Emilia.

368
00:26:30,005 --> 00:26:31,131
Do you hear me?

369
00:26:31,715 --> 00:26:32,799
Do you hear me?

370
00:26:35,593 --> 00:26:39,723
[unsettling music playing]

371
00:26:48,148 --> 00:26:51,526
[music intensifies]

372
00:27:03,955 --> 00:27:08,126
[unsettling music playing]

373
00:27:12,005 --> 00:27:13,048
Let's go, Madrigal.

374
00:27:13,214 --> 00:27:15,467
-Where to, Mayor?
-Miss Aguas.

375
00:27:16,676 --> 00:27:18,511
Does she know we're dropping by?

376
00:27:18,595 --> 00:27:19,721
She might not be there.

377
00:27:21,222 --> 00:27:22,390
I want to surprise her.

378
00:27:24,434 --> 00:27:26,227
Wouldn't that be nice?

379
00:27:26,311 --> 00:27:28,021
You helped her surprise me yourself.

380
00:27:29,314 --> 00:27:30,899
You're right about that, Mayor.

381
00:27:31,274 --> 00:27:32,275
Good.

382
00:27:32,734 --> 00:27:34,527
I'm glad you know your job, Madrigal.

383
00:27:34,819 --> 00:27:36,363
[tense music playing]

384
00:27:36,446 --> 00:27:39,199
I want you to help me
get what I want from Miss Aguas.

385
00:27:41,159 --> 00:27:42,535
-Let's go.
-Yes, Mayor.

386
00:27:58,718 --> 00:28:02,764
[tense music playing]

387
00:28:06,267 --> 00:28:07,602
[car horn honks]

388
00:28:08,728 --> 00:28:11,398
-Hey, Diego!
-[engine stops]

389
00:28:12,482 --> 00:28:14,943
Uncle! What are you doing here?

390
00:28:15,026 --> 00:28:16,903
[chuckles] I was hitching
a ride with Fernan,

391
00:28:16,986 --> 00:28:18,071
but his car broke down.

392
00:28:18,154 --> 00:28:20,782
So, I decided to just walk.
I could use the exercise.

393
00:28:21,199 --> 00:28:24,202
I'm on my way to your place.
Loring got there first.

394
00:28:24,285 --> 00:28:25,787
Are you going somewhere?

395
00:28:26,621 --> 00:28:29,040
That can wait. Let me give you a ride.

396
00:28:29,124 --> 00:28:32,043
No, don't let me keep you.

397
00:28:32,127 --> 00:28:33,420
I think you're going somewhere important.

398
00:28:33,503 --> 00:28:35,588
Of course, I won't let you get tired.

399
00:28:35,672 --> 00:28:39,050
-Come on. Get in.
-Well, if you insist.

400
00:28:42,095 --> 00:28:44,180
[Diego] What happened to the car?

401
00:28:44,264 --> 00:28:45,932
-I'm not sure.
-[engine starts]

402
00:28:46,015 --> 00:28:47,142
It suddenly stopped.

403
00:28:47,934 --> 00:28:49,436
-That's bad.
-[Pandoy chuckles]

404
00:28:49,519 --> 00:28:52,021
You should tell Mr. Fernan
to go buy a new one.

405
00:28:52,105 --> 00:28:53,189
[Pandoy chuckling] I will.

406
00:28:53,940 --> 00:28:54,941
See, this is better than exercise!

407
00:28:55,024 --> 00:28:57,068
I'll just drive you,
so you won't get tired.

408
00:29:02,782 --> 00:29:07,454
[instrumental theme music playing]

409
00:29:21,342 --> 00:29:24,554
Ivy. You have a visitor.

410
00:29:31,394 --> 00:29:32,604
Mr. Mayor.

411
00:29:32,937 --> 00:29:34,898
-Good morning, Miss Aguas.
-Good morning.

412
00:29:35,774 --> 00:29:37,776
To what do I owe the pleasure?

413
00:29:38,443 --> 00:29:41,237
Before anything else, I don't get it.

414
00:29:41,321 --> 00:29:43,907
Why are you becoming
more beautiful every day?

415
00:29:43,990 --> 00:29:45,700
[Ivy chuckles] Thank you.

416
00:29:45,950 --> 00:29:48,161
I'm sure the Congressman
will be happy to see you.

417
00:29:48,995 --> 00:29:50,622
He'll be happy to see me?

418
00:29:50,830 --> 00:29:53,666
I don't remember making
an appointment with him.

419
00:29:53,750 --> 00:29:54,793
You have one now.

420
00:29:55,418 --> 00:29:56,878
I'm sure you don't want to upset him.

421
00:29:56,961 --> 00:29:58,171
So, you'll come, right?

422
00:29:58,296 --> 00:30:01,090
[tense music playing]

423
00:30:01,508 --> 00:30:06,471
Of course! Why would I
turn down Congressman Julio?

424
00:30:07,514 --> 00:30:11,267
So, should I meet him at his house?

425
00:30:12,936 --> 00:30:14,896
You'll find out. Shall we?

426
00:30:15,355 --> 00:30:17,607
Okay. I have to go, Nanny.

427
00:30:17,982 --> 00:30:18,983
All right, Ivy.

428
00:30:19,317 --> 00:30:23,196
[tense music playing]

429
00:30:30,245 --> 00:30:34,082
[soft ominous music playing]

430
00:30:41,548 --> 00:30:44,467
[music intensifies]

431
00:30:47,428 --> 00:30:49,931
<i>I won't let anything happen to you.</i>

432
00:30:50,139 --> 00:30:52,642
<i>I will protect you from my family.</i>

433
00:30:56,896 --> 00:30:59,232
[clicks tongue] Do you think that…

434
00:30:59,649 --> 00:31:02,277
we're doing the right thing
by letting Diego pursue

435
00:31:02,360 --> 00:31:08,658
his feelings for Ivy or Lily,
or whoever that woman is?

436
00:31:09,033 --> 00:31:13,329
Well, Diego's not a kid anymore, Loring.

437
00:31:13,413 --> 00:31:17,166
He's already been through a lot.

438
00:31:17,500 --> 00:31:23,006
Don't you think it's only right
for him to find his happiness?

439
00:31:25,800 --> 00:31:29,596
Not if it will put his life in danger.

440
00:31:29,846 --> 00:31:31,389
[Pandoy clicks tongue, exhales sharply]

441
00:31:32,181 --> 00:31:36,936
It's Diego's decision
to take a risk on love.

442
00:31:37,812 --> 00:31:42,859
All we can do is support him.
If he gets hurt,

443
00:31:42,942 --> 00:31:48,531
then let's stay by his side
until he recovers from the pain.

444
00:31:49,699 --> 00:31:51,534
[sighs deeply]

445
00:31:57,290 --> 00:31:58,291
[Pandoy exhales]

446
00:32:03,796 --> 00:32:05,006
Congressman Julio!

447
00:32:05,089 --> 00:32:08,718
Welcome back! It's nice to see you back.

448
00:32:09,302 --> 00:32:11,804
It's nice to be back, Miss Aguas.

449
00:32:11,888 --> 00:32:12,972
Please, sit down.

450
00:32:13,723 --> 00:32:14,724
Thank you.

451
00:32:14,974 --> 00:32:17,810
-Would you care for some tea?
-No, I'm good. Thank you.

452
00:32:19,228 --> 00:32:21,773
So, where's Emilia?

453
00:32:22,398 --> 00:32:26,694
[chuckles] Emilia doesn't need
to be part of this conversation.

454
00:32:27,070 --> 00:32:30,698
Actually, I'm more interested
in your report

455
00:32:30,782 --> 00:32:35,745
about our supposed projects and plans.

456
00:32:35,995 --> 00:32:36,996
Supposedly.

457
00:32:37,080 --> 00:32:38,957
[chuckles] You want me
to deliver the report?

458
00:32:39,082 --> 00:32:41,042
Congressman, I shouldn't
be the one doing that.

459
00:32:41,709 --> 00:32:43,419
Arnaldo can do it himself.

460
00:32:44,212 --> 00:32:46,047
Actually, he already did.

461
00:32:46,756 --> 00:32:48,132
He already told me everything,

462
00:32:48,216 --> 00:32:51,970
especially about how
you helped the farmers.

463
00:32:54,389 --> 00:32:55,890
-[Ivy] <i>Stop!</i>
-[Arnaldo] <i>Miss Aguas!</i>

464
00:32:55,974 --> 00:32:57,141
-[Arnaldo] <i>Miss Aguas!</i>
-[Pandoy] <i>Butchoy!</i>

465
00:32:57,225 --> 00:32:58,726
-[Ivy] <i>Stop!</i>
<i>-Butchoy, what are you doing?</i>

466
00:32:58,810 --> 00:32:59,978
<i>It's okay. It's okay.</i>

467
00:33:00,061 --> 00:33:03,648
<i>Mr. Mayor, make them stop!</i>
<i>There's an innocent child here!</i>

468
00:33:04,482 --> 00:33:07,193
[Julio] <i>Aside from that,</i>
<i>you transferred the EPZ site,</i>

469
00:33:07,652 --> 00:33:10,279
<i>and you even bought</i>
<i>the land for the farmers.</i>

470
00:33:10,363 --> 00:33:13,658
[Pandoy] <i>Thank you so much.</i>
<i>We are forever indebted to you.</i>

471
00:33:13,741 --> 00:33:15,868
[Fernan] <i>He's right, Miss Ivy.</i>
<i>You've been helping us</i>

472
00:33:15,952 --> 00:33:17,870
<i>ever since the dispersal.</i>

473
00:33:17,954 --> 00:33:18,955
[farmer] <i>That's right.</i>

474
00:33:22,041 --> 00:33:24,252
[clicks tongue] Admirable.

475
00:33:25,586 --> 00:33:29,549
By the way, I also heard
that you had some dealings

476
00:33:29,632 --> 00:33:32,552
with my late friend, Pablo.

477
00:33:34,220 --> 00:33:37,473
Would it be all right if I ask
what you two talked about?

478
00:33:38,266 --> 00:33:40,643
Uh… Does it have something to do…

479
00:33:42,020 --> 00:33:43,771
with the plan to bring me down?

480
00:33:43,938 --> 00:33:45,898
[both laugh]

481
00:33:45,982 --> 00:33:48,901
Congressman… I see you're
still good at cracking jokes.

482
00:33:50,319 --> 00:33:52,238
[sighs] Nothing like that, Congressman.

483
00:33:53,364 --> 00:33:59,078
The truth is I wanted to support
Arnaldo in his decision

484
00:33:59,162 --> 00:34:00,872
to take over your position.

485
00:34:01,914 --> 00:34:05,043
But then, you know how Emilia is.

486
00:34:05,626 --> 00:34:08,046
You've probably heard about what she did.

487
00:34:09,380 --> 00:34:14,135
I heard. Well, you'll
have to excuse Arnaldo.

488
00:34:14,218 --> 00:34:16,137
He didn't have the heart
to push through with it.

489
00:34:16,554 --> 00:34:22,435
He has a lot to learn about
being a go-getter, like me.

490
00:34:24,437 --> 00:34:25,480
You know, Miss Aguas…

491
00:34:26,314 --> 00:34:29,025
You should give me
the money you promised me.

492
00:34:29,442 --> 00:34:33,196
I mean, we should join forces.

493
00:34:33,571 --> 00:34:35,823
Can you imagine what we can achieve?

494
00:34:36,365 --> 00:34:39,118
With your wealth and my influence.

495
00:34:39,202 --> 00:34:42,413
[tense music playing]

496
00:34:44,373 --> 00:34:48,252
You want me to give it so soon?
You just got back, Congressman.

497
00:34:49,253 --> 00:34:51,464
I see Emilia really does take after you.

498
00:34:52,048 --> 00:34:53,049
[chuckles lightly]

499
00:34:53,299 --> 00:34:57,136
The election's still far off.
Now's not the time.

500
00:34:58,262 --> 00:34:59,680
There's a right time for that.

501
00:35:02,725 --> 00:35:06,020
I have to go, Congressman.
Enjoy your breakfast.

502
00:35:06,979 --> 00:35:08,231
Good morning, Miss Aguas.

503
00:35:11,192 --> 00:35:13,986
[tense music playing]

504
00:35:17,448 --> 00:35:18,574
[sighs]

505
00:35:20,159 --> 00:35:22,495
Grandpa. Where's Ivy?

506
00:35:23,204 --> 00:35:24,330
[Julio] Hmm.

507
00:35:24,664 --> 00:35:28,584
[tense music intensifies]

508
00:35:39,303 --> 00:35:40,388
[music fades]

509
00:35:43,057 --> 00:35:45,518
[Emilia] Hello, Raul? Listen to me.

510
00:35:45,852 --> 00:35:47,812
Don't come to the house just yet.

511
00:35:47,895 --> 00:35:50,565
I'm sure Papa will have you killed.

512
00:35:51,023 --> 00:35:54,277
You better stay at your
parents' place in San Ildefonso.

513
00:35:54,861 --> 00:35:56,571
Don't come here. I'll go to you…

514
00:35:56,654 --> 00:35:58,489
<i>when things have settled down here.</i>

515
00:35:59,282 --> 00:36:00,825
Emilia, that's not the best idea.

516
00:36:01,159 --> 00:36:02,785
Your father can still find me there.

517
00:36:03,452 --> 00:36:05,496
Besides, I've found
another place to stay at.

518
00:36:06,247 --> 00:36:07,665
That's good, then.

519
00:36:08,332 --> 00:36:11,419
Raul, you have to help me bring down Papa.

520
00:36:11,878 --> 00:36:14,714
Otherwise, he'll have both our heads.

521
00:36:15,631 --> 00:36:17,842
Please, Emilia. Stop this.

522
00:36:17,925 --> 00:36:20,928
Don't drag me into those
stupid plans of yours.

523
00:36:25,266 --> 00:36:27,059
[grunts, sighs]

524
00:36:27,518 --> 00:36:28,477
Hmm!

525
00:36:36,861 --> 00:36:41,991
<i>San Ildefonso. The Torillos' old house.</i>

526
00:36:42,992 --> 00:36:46,204
<i>That's where Raul</i>
<i>could be hiding my mother.</i>

527
00:36:51,250 --> 00:36:52,251
[sighs]

528
00:36:59,717 --> 00:37:01,385
<i>Everything will go back to normal.</i>

529
00:37:02,678 --> 00:37:07,266
<i>Even if it's just us. You and me.</i>

530
00:37:08,768 --> 00:37:12,521
<i>I'll take care of you. I won't lose you.</i>

531
00:37:17,818 --> 00:37:20,780
[dramatic tense music playing]

532
00:37:32,375 --> 00:37:35,419
[dramatic tense music playing]

533
00:37:39,423 --> 00:37:44,470
Why? Did you think
we could get it that easy?

534
00:37:46,138 --> 00:37:48,724
That woman will make us work for it.

535
00:37:53,688 --> 00:37:56,190
You know, Arnaldo, I have a suspicion

536
00:37:57,566 --> 00:38:00,027
that Miss Aguas is hiding something.

537
00:38:03,406 --> 00:38:05,157
I want you to follow her.

538
00:38:07,785 --> 00:38:09,829
Find out where she goes.

539
00:38:13,541 --> 00:38:16,585
Yes, Grandpa. Madrigal, let's go.

540
00:38:32,310 --> 00:38:35,896
<i>Where are you going, Ivy?</i>
<i>Who are you looking for?</i>

541
00:38:41,444 --> 00:38:44,238
<i>Diego? Why is he following me?</i>

542
00:38:50,119 --> 00:38:53,998
[tense music playing]

543
00:39:02,673 --> 00:39:03,799
Faster, Madrigal.

544
00:39:04,550 --> 00:39:06,177
We need to know where Ivy's going.

545
00:39:06,260 --> 00:39:08,387
She might meet my good-for-nothing dad

546
00:39:08,471 --> 00:39:10,431
to plan something against Grandpa.

547
00:39:10,848 --> 00:39:11,932
Yes, Mayor.

548
00:39:12,016 --> 00:39:15,353
WE ARE FOLLOWING YOU.

549
00:39:15,436 --> 00:39:16,395
[phone chimes]

550
00:39:21,275 --> 00:39:22,693
<i>You too, Arnaldo?</i>

551
00:39:23,986 --> 00:39:25,821
<i>Why are they following me?</i>

552
00:39:33,621 --> 00:39:34,789
There! Follow her car.

553
00:39:35,706 --> 00:39:36,707
Mayor, we'll take the other road.

554
00:39:36,791 --> 00:39:38,167
There's an intersection at the end.

555
00:39:38,250 --> 00:39:39,668
We can catch her there.

556
00:39:39,752 --> 00:39:40,753
What?

557
00:39:41,170 --> 00:39:45,633
[tense music playing]

558
00:39:56,352 --> 00:39:57,353
Where is she?

559
00:39:58,938 --> 00:40:00,648
-[clicks tongue, sighs]
-Where's Ivy?!

560
00:40:01,399 --> 00:40:04,235
Damn it, Madrigal!
I told you not to lose her!

561
00:40:04,777 --> 00:40:07,154
Mayor, I'm sorry. It was my mistake.

562
00:40:07,238 --> 00:40:08,823
Did you do it intentionally?!

563
00:40:10,282 --> 00:40:13,869
[tense music playing]

564
00:40:17,706 --> 00:40:19,583
[Arnaldo breathes heavily]

565
00:40:21,085 --> 00:40:24,964
<i>It's important that I can trust</i>
<i>my staff, Madrigal.</i>

566
00:40:26,048 --> 00:40:30,177
<i>Your loyalty should only</i>
<i>be to me and my family.</i>

567
00:40:31,137 --> 00:40:34,807
<i>Because if not, you might end up dead.</i>

568
00:40:36,225 --> 00:40:38,811
<i>It would be a shame if that happens.</i>

569
00:40:53,659 --> 00:40:54,994
[footsteps fading]

570
00:41:01,167 --> 00:41:02,168
[exhales]

571
00:41:07,256 --> 00:41:09,717
[breathing heavily]

572
00:41:09,800 --> 00:41:10,718
[groans]

573
00:41:11,844 --> 00:41:12,845
[Camia groans]

574
00:41:13,053 --> 00:41:16,182
-Jasmin. What's wrong?
-[Camia groaning]

575
00:41:16,265 --> 00:41:18,267
-What's wrong?
-[groaning]

576
00:41:18,350 --> 00:41:21,228
Jasmin, what's wrong? Hold on.

577
00:41:21,479 --> 00:41:25,983
Where are you going?
Jasmin, wait! Love, stop.

578
00:41:26,066 --> 00:41:28,819
Where are you going? You can't go outside.

579
00:41:29,195 --> 00:41:30,321
[grunts]

580
00:41:30,404 --> 00:41:33,073
-Come. Sit down. Tell me.
-[groaning]

581
00:41:33,491 --> 00:41:35,326
What's wrong? Tell me.

582
00:41:35,409 --> 00:41:37,578
-[groaning]
-Tell me.

583
00:41:37,661 --> 00:41:42,625
Where does it hurt? Your stomach?

584
00:41:43,000 --> 00:41:44,001
Hmm?

585
00:41:44,084 --> 00:41:45,961
[Camia sobbing, grunting]

586
00:41:46,045 --> 00:41:49,423
All right. Listen to me.
This is what we'll do.

587
00:41:49,882 --> 00:41:56,388
I'll go outside to buy medicine,
but I need to lock you up here.

588
00:41:56,764 --> 00:41:58,933
I want you to be safe. I'm sorry, love.

589
00:42:01,352 --> 00:42:03,395
There's food there if you want to eat.

590
00:42:03,479 --> 00:42:04,605
I'll be back soon.

591
00:42:05,564 --> 00:42:08,067
[sobbing, gasping]

592
00:42:09,235 --> 00:42:12,780
[Camia groaning]

593
00:42:13,489 --> 00:42:15,324
[Camia gasping]

594
00:42:19,912 --> 00:42:22,414
[Camia gasping]

595
00:42:28,295 --> 00:42:30,464
[breathes heavily]

596
00:42:35,261 --> 00:42:38,722
[tense music playing]

597
00:42:41,934 --> 00:42:42,893
[car unlocks]

598
00:42:49,858 --> 00:42:51,777
[breathing heavily]

599
00:42:58,284 --> 00:43:02,329
[sobbing]

600
00:43:07,960 --> 00:43:11,422
[wailing]

601
00:43:12,172 --> 00:43:14,925
<i>Anyone who opposes me will be punished.</i>

602
00:43:15,593 --> 00:43:19,263
<i>And you, Emilia, I'll make you suffer.</i>

603
00:43:20,180 --> 00:43:25,019
<i>You'll see just how</i>
<i>cruel your father can be.</i>

604
00:43:29,064 --> 00:43:31,900
[wailing]

605
00:43:31,984 --> 00:43:33,527
[squeals]

606
00:43:33,944 --> 00:43:36,113
[wailing, screaming]

607
00:43:36,196 --> 00:43:37,197
[glass shatters]

608
00:43:38,115 --> 00:43:40,826
[wailing]

609
00:43:42,620 --> 00:43:46,540
[wailing]

610
00:43:47,708 --> 00:43:48,709
Emilia!

611
00:43:50,794 --> 00:43:53,756
[sobbing] Auntie…

612
00:43:53,839 --> 00:43:56,759
-[suspenseful music playing]
-[Emilia sobbing]

613
00:43:56,884 --> 00:43:59,845
Emilia, you aren't alone in
your fight against your father.

614
00:44:00,721 --> 00:44:01,889
I'm here for you.

615
00:44:02,806 --> 00:44:05,809
We will bring him down by whatever means!

616
00:44:06,769 --> 00:44:07,978
Do you understand me?

617
00:44:10,105 --> 00:44:11,607
I promise you that.

618
00:44:11,857 --> 00:44:16,070
[suspenseful music playing]

619
00:44:16,153 --> 00:44:18,155
[sobs]

620
00:44:30,959 --> 00:44:32,378
I'm here, Emilia.

621
00:44:35,297 --> 00:44:38,175
[Emilia sobbing]

622
00:44:39,093 --> 00:44:42,721
[tense music playing]

623
00:44:42,971 --> 00:44:44,807
[Emilia sobbing]

624
00:44:53,565 --> 00:44:57,778
[tense music intensifies]

625
00:45:04,618 --> 00:45:06,161
[Emilia sobbing]

626
00:45:07,579 --> 00:45:11,041
The Torillos' residence?
Oh, they're well-known here.

627
00:45:11,458 --> 00:45:14,294
Mr. Torillo is Congressman
Ardiente's best friend…

628
00:45:14,711 --> 00:45:16,922
while his son became
Governor Emilia's husband.

629
00:45:17,798 --> 00:45:22,136
I see. Is their house still far from here?

630
00:45:22,469 --> 00:45:26,098
It is. I'd say around a two-hour ride.

631
00:45:26,348 --> 00:45:27,933
You can find it beyond those fields.

632
00:45:29,768 --> 00:45:30,936
How do I get there?

633
00:45:31,437 --> 00:45:35,357
Go straight ahead, and you'll
eventually see a steep road.

634
00:45:35,732 --> 00:45:38,569
There, you'll find
an old lone house there.

635
00:45:38,777 --> 00:45:40,988
But I'm not sure
if anyone still lives in it.

636
00:45:41,530 --> 00:45:42,823
All right, thank you.

637
00:45:48,704 --> 00:45:50,205
[engine starts]

638
00:46:01,341 --> 00:46:03,760
[suspenseful music playing]

639
00:46:07,931 --> 00:46:10,809
[doorbell ringing]

640
00:46:13,061 --> 00:46:14,313
Hey, Diego.

641
00:46:14,813 --> 00:46:17,858
-Has Ivy come home yet?
-Not yet.

642
00:46:18,317 --> 00:46:20,486
Did she tell you what time
she'll be coming back?

643
00:46:21,236 --> 00:46:22,738
Is there a problem, Diego?

644
00:46:23,530 --> 00:46:25,574
Do you remember
what I told you last night?

645
00:46:25,866 --> 00:46:29,453
Don't worry. I won't leave
until she comes back.

646
00:46:30,954 --> 00:46:33,290
Okay. Come inside. Wait here.

647
00:46:39,338 --> 00:46:40,172
-[mugs clinking]
-Oh, no!

648
00:46:40,255 --> 00:46:41,173
-[mugs break]
-Oh, no!

649
00:46:41,256 --> 00:46:42,007
-What--
-My goodness!

650
00:46:42,090 --> 00:46:43,217
-I knew it! Good grief!
-Goodness, Loring!

651
00:46:43,300 --> 00:46:44,301
I knew it!

652
00:46:44,384 --> 00:46:46,011
-Loring, snap out of it.
-My gut is telling me

653
00:46:46,094 --> 00:46:47,346
that something bad is going to happen!

654
00:46:47,429 --> 00:46:48,680
Loring. Loring. Loring.

655
00:46:49,765 --> 00:46:52,184
Loring, nothing bad is going to happen!

656
00:46:52,267 --> 00:46:58,148
You dropped that because you got
clumsy from worrying so much.

657
00:47:00,943 --> 00:47:02,653
Can you blame me?

658
00:47:09,618 --> 00:47:11,662
[Carlotta] Diego, have a seat.

659
00:47:11,745 --> 00:47:13,830
I'll get you something to drink, okay?

660
00:47:13,914 --> 00:47:15,582
-Okay, thank you.
-Okay.

661
00:47:23,090 --> 00:47:25,717
[tense music playing]

662
00:47:29,930 --> 00:47:32,683
[tense music intensifies]

663
00:47:43,860 --> 00:47:47,990
[tense music playing]

664
00:47:52,035 --> 00:47:53,996
[dramatic music]

665
00:47:59,084 --> 00:48:01,044
[young Lily] The Count of Monte Cristo.

666
00:48:01,128 --> 00:48:03,797
<i>I love it when my father reads this to me.</i>

667
00:48:03,880 --> 00:48:05,340
<i>Do you know </i>The Count of Monte Cristo<i>?</i>

668
00:48:05,424 --> 00:48:07,175
<i>It's an amazing book.</i>

669
00:48:12,055 --> 00:48:15,475
[tense music playing]

670
00:48:20,439 --> 00:48:24,109
[tense music playing]

671
00:48:37,789 --> 00:48:41,627
<i>Pa, the people at the office</i>
<i>are very happy that you're back.</i>

672
00:48:41,710 --> 00:48:43,629
<i>What about you, Emilia? Are you happy?</i>

673
00:48:43,712 --> 00:48:46,965
<i>-Of course, Papa. I'm--</i>
<i>-Don't lie to me!</i>

674
00:48:47,049 --> 00:48:50,385
<i>Tonight, all your lies</i>
<i>will come to an end!</i>

675
00:48:50,552 --> 00:48:52,929
[Diego] <i>I'm sure of it. That girl is Lily.</i>

676
00:48:53,013 --> 00:48:54,514
<i>I need to know the truth.</i>

677
00:48:54,640 --> 00:48:57,017
-<i>Mom, are you here?</i>
-[Camia screams]

678
00:48:57,100 --> 00:48:58,101
[dishes shatter]

679
00:48:58,393 --> 00:48:59,936
[grunts] <i>Mom!</i>

680
00:49:00,771 --> 00:49:03,732
[sobs] <i>Mom. Mom! Mom. Mom.</i>

681
00:49:05,025 --> 00:49:08,862
<i>Love, what is it? Is there</i>
<i>something you want to tell me?</i>

682
00:49:11,114 --> 00:49:13,909
[theme music playing]
